Wow well what a night so many friends  and family and people we've worked with  over the years I kind of feel like I'm  having my bar mitzvah we're a little bit  of a roast from Steven but thank you all  again for coming tonight it's just a  joyous evening and Thank You Steven and  Matt for those kind words and thanks to  the Academy we're really thrilled to be  here tonight and we'd like to also  congratulate Cicely Tyson Lila chephren  and Marvin levy on their Oscar  and one special shout-out for our dear  friend Marvin Marvin happy birthday well  there you are because we are the first  couple to receive this honor I guess  it's only fitting that I began my career  in movies working for another creative  couple Peter Bogdanovich and Polly Platt  I had met them at a party in 1966 for  John Ford's daughter Barbara who was a  film editor and was married to Ken  Curtis  one of Ford's repertory of actors and a  good friend of my parents Peter and  Polly were in town doing a documentary  on mr. Ford and Peter was very excited  that night because a producer named  Roger Corman had just offered him his  first directing job it wasn't going to  happen right away because they still had  no script and they'd had to write it and  then they would do that back in New York  now despite the fact I was majoring in  political science at UCLA as everyone  was back then and despite the fact I  knew nothing about movies I offered to  you I offered to help Peter and Polly if  they ever came back and sure enough  about three months later my dad called  and said did you meet a guy named box  Lana vich or something at the fort party  and I said yes why he wants you to call  him for those under 30 that was how  social media worked back then someone  would call your dad on a landline leave  a message  he would write it down in a couple of  weeks later he might remember to tell  you to call that person back  so I called Peter back and he said he  and Polly were going to make this movie  called targets and would I be interested  in working on it I said can I start in  an hour and then I asked well what would  you want me to do he answered I don't  know I've never made a movie before  just come over so I did and without  knowing it I began to learn the skills  that a producer needs to solve problems  and I began to understand the challenges  in helping the director get their vision  up on the screen and this could not have  been a better starting point for me in  becoming a creative producer because  with Peter as the director and Polly as  the production designer I got to see and  solve problems from the creative side  targets was an on-the-job film school  and the best introduction the filmmaking  one could ever have I watched Peter  block and set up shots and how  brilliantly he worked with the actors  and I learned from Polly how our  producer should be hands-on in paying  attention to detail and these first  on-the-job lessons I got from them have  stayed with me to this day now I know  you're wondering about that political  science degree well I did graduate from  UCLA and was on my way to law school  when I realized I had fall in love with  the process of making movies luckily  Peter rescued me from what might have  been a very unhappy legal career when he  called and again and asked me to come to  Texas for the last picture show I  immediately accepted the job of location  manager and that's who led to being  promoted to associate producer on Paper  Moon for the rest of the 70s I was lucky  to do several more pictures with Peter  and three other visionary directors  Walter Hill one of them  and a couple of other guys named Orson  Welles and Martin Scorsese but they're  not here tonight and I was also lucky to  be mentored by legendary producers Larry  Gordon who was here tonight  Irwin Winkler and George Lucas and on  the personal side I was single and  happily married to the movies that I was  making and then in 1979 Steven changed  all that when he hired Kathy to be his  secretary assistant on Raiders of the  Lost Ark I never dreamed I would meet  someone who loved making movies as much  as I did but working with Steven Kathy  and I became friends and collaborators  and eventually we became an actual  family thank you all again for this  wonderful honor and celebration and  thanks to all the producers and  directors who have given us this  opportunity to take this joyful journey  together and pursue the passion we love  making movies and telling stories and in  particular thank you to Peter  Bogdanovich for his trust and loyalty in  me we're still working together half a  century later after he took a chance on  me and how fitting is it for us to have  just produced our tenth picture together  the completion of Orson Welles his final  film the other side of the wind  and now I'm going to pass the baton to  my partner in movies and in life  Kathleen Kennedy  yeah I'm not sure I'm going to recover  from the couch story yes well I have to  say it's pretty amazing to be standing  here obviously with Frank and Steven and  realizing that we now join the company  of so many greats that have received  this award in the past filmmakers such  as William Wyler Jack Warner Stephen  Francis Coppola Alfred Hitchcock George  Lucas legends all and both of us are  very proud that you find us worthy to be  honored as part of this Hollywood legacy  it also means a lot to have both Matt  and Steven here to present the award to  us I don't know what happened to Matt  but I think he's still here  and we're very honored to share the  Thalberg award as the first married  couple I'm also very proud to be the  first woman to accept this award  but I'm also not the first to deserve it  and I'm a hundred percent sure I'm not  the last I've always loved the movies  and I've been enthralled by the power of  story Stephen said this when he accepted  the award 30 years ago that power begins  with the written word  I feel extraordinarily lucky to have  worked with some of the best  screenwriters and directors in the  business and also to have witnessed so  many advances in technology to help tell  those stories but those advances are  only made powerful and emotional in  their support of storytelling that pluie  blueprint those words set everything in  motion and without great writing we have  nothing to produce  when I began working with Stephen he  handed me a script for his next film he  said read this it's my next movie but  don't tell anybody anything and that  directive is pretty much what he tells  you every time he hands you anything  that script was Raiders of the Lost Ark  written by Lawrence Kasdan and remains  today one of the best scripts I've ever  read when I finished this reading the  script Steven was waiting expectantly to  hear what I thought I said it's great  but how are we gonna make this and he  said call producer Frank Marshall so I  called mr. Marshall I called him mr.  Marshall repeatedly until he said could  you please stop calling me that I'm  Frank he then offered to come over to  our offices and introduce himself I was  expecting this much older man maybe  mid-50s but in walked this handsome  young guy and I have to admit my first  reaction was hello mr. Marshall  [Applause]  so after some back-and-forth I told  Frank that Stephen asked me to build  some models of the truck chase in  Raiders but I confessed I hadn't done  much model building Frank was  immediately excited and agreed to help  me he loved building models so to quote  Humphrey Bogart's line in clot to Claude  Rains in Casablanca it was the beginning  of a beautiful friendship that  friendship is now actually in its 32nd  year of marriage and 40 and 40 years of  collaboration and I'm so grateful to  share a career and a home with someone  whose character and convictions his  decency and humor are an evidence every  day and as proud as we are of our movies  we have two wonderful daughters who are  the heart and soul of our lives  [Applause]  when they were little we would throw  them into backpacks and carry them  through the redwoods while making  Jurassic Park or sometimes we would  create school rooms on the set of  Indiana Jones and during our time away  we have worked tirelessly in tandem to  watch them grow and to make sure that  their lives are defined by creativity  quality and most of all kindness these  are the same values we bring to our  filmmaking and the same values the  Thalberg award must always continue to  represent I've been fortunate to have  had the chance to work with  extraordinary people to help reinforce  those ideals my mother my father Frank  and of course Steven Steven Frank and I  formed Amblin entertainment in 1981 with  a goal that I think would make mr.  Thalberg proud to tell hopeful story  stories about triumphs of the human  spirit and the ability to rise above  circumstance and even with all the  exciting changes happening within film  and motion pictures with all the tools  being invented that helped us tell those  stories those fundamental values that I  look for and strive for will never  change but we all know there are changes  in our industry that should be embraced  ones that must be embraced for as our  industry grows and changes who gets to  tell their stories needs to grow and  change as well  I know firsthand how allowing new voices  at the table can change someone's life  my opportunity to work in television was  the result of a lawsuit back in 1973  filed against a station because women  did not occupy any technical jobs that  lawsuit opened the door for me and it is  just one reason why I so passionately  believe that each of us has the  obligation to ensure that everyone who  has a story to tell be given the  opportunity that I and many of you in  this room had and it is my hope that  with this inclusion of these powerful  new voices we might just bring the world  back to its senses just and maybe just  maybe shatter a few glass ceilings along  the way  so tonight to end this I just want to  say we are profoundly grateful to be  here tonight with all of you and I mean  it's just incredible that Oprah is here  and Quincy is here and we've worked with  Marvin levy and Stephens here and it  feels like some kind of amazing reunion  that I can't quite believe the stars  wind up in quite the way they did but  there's nothing that's more important  than to be able to experience something  like this with people that you genuinely  care about and have been a part of your  life for a long time so this is an  incredible honor and a privilege and we  thank you  [Applause]
 

